.TH SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SESSION_ID_STRING 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SESSION_ID_STRING \- The session ID string used for saving and restoring window state across runs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_video.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_PROP_GLOBAL_VIDEO_WAYLAND_SESSION_ID_STRING \(dqSDL.video.wayland.session_id\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This requires that the compositor supports the
.BR xdg_session_management_v1
protocol\[char46]
.PP
To save and restore the current state of Wayland toplevel windows, set this to a non-null value before creating a window, and serialize this value before shutting down\[char46] To restore the previous state on subsequent runs, set this property to the previously serialized value before window creation\[char46]
.PP
This can be set at any time before the first call to a window creation function\[char46] Reading should be deferred until serialization time, as compositors may not set the session identifier string immediately, and the identifier string may change during runtime, so it should not be cached\[char46]
.PP
Setting this to an empty string (\(dq\(dq) before creating a window will cause a new session with an automatically generated identifier string to be created\[char46]
.PP
Setting this to null or an empty string before shutting down the video subsystem will cause the existing session to be removed\[char46]
.PP
Note that for windows to be saved/restored by the session, they also need a stable, unique identifier string set via the
.BR SDL_PROP_WINDOW_CREATE_WAYLAND_WINDOW_ID_STRING
property at creation time\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This property is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

